{
  "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
  "id": "10283",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10283",
  "key": "AIN-54",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Data model] Deliver additive schema migrations, legacy backfills and reconciliation reports",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Parent owns shared data-model implementation. Planning priority: foundational. Preserve existing behavior through additive changes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Current state"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Models have historical/seeded records, missing currency or lineage, nullable ownership and multiple package owners. Existing immutable financial evidence must not be rewritten or inferred into false certainty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Deliverables and acceptance criteria"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Create an expand/backfill/validate/cutover plan with service/package compatibility order and idempotent batches."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Classify unresolved ownership/currency/version fields explicitly; require reviewed mapping or quarantine instead of fabricated defaults."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Rehearse migration and application rollback on representative legacy snapshots; compare row counts, keys and financial totals by currency/party and retain audit reports."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Related domain work"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "AIN-14, AIN-18, AIN-34, AIN-35. Coordinate contracts with these tickets; do not reimplement their business workflows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Remaining finance obligations after Network/marketplace delivery \u2014 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "As a release operator, I need rehearsed additive migrations and reviewed backfills so financial history survives deployment and rollback."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Include the Network identity-link and marketplace participant-review/commitment-receipt migrations in service/package compatibility order. These migrations were tested only in disposable Docker databases. Remaining: representative legacy migration, evidenced ownership/currency mappings or quarantine, repeatable reconciliation reports, staged cutover and application rollback/restore rehearsal. Preserve immutable evidence; no destructive rollback or guessed financial defaults."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Verification required before Done: preserve original acceptance criteria and all required dependencies/subtasks. Every new or changed user workflow must have a linked user story and executable Storybook play scenarios for success, validation, denied/stale, loading/error and retry as applicable. Run real-service journeys against isolated Docker containers for persistence, authorization, concurrency and money invariants. Provider settlement requires actual configured sandbox evidence; Docker simulations alone do not establish cash settlement. Record story IDs, commands/results, limitations, migration and deployment status. No implementation or release completion is claimed by this planning update."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Single-developer sprint sequence \u2014 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Target candidate: AIN S54 | Legacy migration rehearsal (Jira sprint 89)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sprint outcome: Rehearse additive migrations/backfills and compatible application cutover on representative legacy data."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Exit evidence: All delivered migrations, including identity/participation additions, have reviewed mappings or quarantine; idempotent batches and rollback preserve immutable history."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Planning envelope: 6 implementation days + 2 integrated verification days + 1 review/refinement day + 1 contingency day; not measured velocity. One primary outcome in progress; at most two closely related workflow slices. Story/task pairs share effort, not double-counted work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing active sprint remains active with original dates; only its goal/name and unfinished membership are reorganized. Every new sprint is future and undated. No fabricated story-point/time estimates or assignees. The ordered slots are a provisional work breakdown, not a fixed delivery forecast. Before activation, split any candidate exceeding six implementation days and verify reviewer/provider readiness; preserve all parent acceptance criteria."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scheduling is not implementation: original AC/DoD and parent scope are unchanged. Related story/task/subtask effort is one delivery slice, not additive capacity. Required domain slices can be delivered earlier than the broader owner completion sprint; no broader item is Done until all original requirements pass."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
